# playpick gave mode=battleground map=conquest spec=druid:balance style=good
# view=820x1180,touch save=carried. direction.md's #7 ("a battleground does not
# carry a passive body the way a raid does") has an open question: two prior
# good-style/auto-fallback attempts (flags/druid:feral, escort/warlock:destruction)
# both died within 15s and never got to test whether active play helps, because
# the body couldn't survive contact at all. This is the third map (conquest,
# The Three Cairns -- hold ground, clock does the rest) and the first `good`
# attempt on it. druid:balance is ranged/caster like the two priors, not melee,
# so if it also dies immediately that is a third data point toward "good dies
# fast on a battleground regardless of map," and if it survives, this is the
# first chance to see whether active play actually turns one of these losses
# around.
